\title{Tautologies and contradictions}
\date{2026-01-28T21:16:01Z}
\tag{discrete}
\taxon{Definition}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{A [proposition](002O) that is always true, no matter the values of the propositional variables it contains, is a \em{tautology}.  One that is always false is a \em{contradiction}.}
